<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Sexi</h1><p class="st-meta">800 BCE – 206 BCE (approx.) · capital Sexi</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Phoenician colony at Almuñécar on Spain's southern coast, known for its rich tombs and for salted fish exported across the Mediterranean.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Sexi was founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phoenicians">Phoenicians</a> in the 8th century BCE on the headland of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almunecar">Almuñécar</a>, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> province. It formed part of the string of Phoenician harbours along the Andalusian coast, between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/malaka">Malaka</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/abdera">Abdera</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Its Laurita necropolis has yielded Egyptian alabaster vases reused as burial urns, evidence of the colonists' wide contacts. The city's economy rested on trade and on fish salting, and its later Punic-legend coins carried tuna, the source of its wealth. Its government is not recorded.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>With the Roman conquest of the south after 206 BCE, Sexi passed under Roman control. It kept its fish-salting industry and became the Roman town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almunecar">Firmum Iulium Sexi</a>, ancestor of modern Almuñécar.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 800 BCE – 206 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Iberia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:43.78%;width:11.82%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>800 BCE – 206 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century-bce">9th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Sexi</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Phoenician religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Phoenician</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Almunecar</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-503&amp;focus=sexi" aria-label="Sexi on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4588 854 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sexi lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4908 1110L5259 1106"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5259 1106h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4908 1110h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4908 1110h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Sexi. <a href="/atlas?year=-503&amp;focus=sexi">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

